WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.667
These are the key contracts.

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:05.617
Scalar means one value. IN means membership.

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:11.087
EXISTS means existence. ANY and ALL compare one value with a set.

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:15.472
Correlation means the inner query depends on the current outer row.

00:00:15.472 --> 00:00:21.137
A derived table means the inner query produces rows for the outer query to use.

00:00:21.137 --> 00:00:25.507
If you understand the meaning, you can rebuild the syntax when needed.

00:00:25.507 --> 00:00:30.887
Connect this idea to a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists.

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:36.057
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:43.182
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.182 --> 00:00:48.577
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:53.760
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
